    <string name="reliability_title">Keeping the monitoring running</string>
    <string name="reliability_intro">To avoid missing payment notifications, we recommend: turn off battery optimization for this app, do not let Android remove its permissions, and never use \"Force stop\". On Samsung phones also make sure the app is not in \"Sleeping apps\" or \"Deep sleeping apps\".</string>
    <string name="reliability_battery_card_title">Battery optimization is on</string>
    <string name="reliability_battery_card_body">Android restricts this app in the background, so it may miss notifications. Set Butterfly III to \"Don\'t optimize\" (or \"Unrestricted\").</string>
    <string name="reliability_battery_button">Open battery optimization settings</string>
    <string name="reliability_autorevoke_card_title">Permissions may be removed</string>
    <string name="reliability_autorevoke_card_body">If you do not open the app for a long time, Android can remove its permissions and stop it. Turn off \"Remove permissions if app isn\'t used\" (the name differs between phones).</string>
    <string name="reliability_autorevoke_button">Open app permission settings</string>
    <string name="reliability_app_info_button">Open app info…</string>
    <string name="test_match_issue_account_approximate">⚠ The account in this rule is a guess - automatic creation is skipped and duplicates are checked without comparing accounts.</string>
    <string name="rule_field_account_approximate">Account is a guess</string>
    <string name="rule_field_account_approximate_hint">Turn this on when the notification does not say which account or card was used, so the account above is only a guess. The app then never creates the transaction by itself: it asks you to review it. It also recognises the same payment reported by another app that knows the account (for example your wallet), and drops its own reminder. Duplicates are found by amount and time only.</string>
    <string name="notification_rule_line">Rule: %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_diagnostic_switch">Write diagnostic log</string>
    <string name="about_diagnostic_hint">Off by default. When on, the app writes short technical notes about what it decided for each message: your rule names, times, Firefly transaction numbers and a short fingerprint of each amount (enough to compare two) - but not the amounts, descriptions or account names. Turning it off deletes the notes. Copy them if you report a problem.</string>
